From 259b2bff6876679d6c5b9acd6c2cc2d14e0f3108 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HempFiend <17104973+jaidenscool1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 08:35:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 36/37] nx2: passthrough backend: washed-out race frames:
 measuring switches, upload store (opt-in)

Sole mode shows overexposed race frames in 3-10% of shots in every configuration
(Vulkan none). Measuring and experimental switches, all off by default:
- EDEN_NX2_PASSTHROUGH_BACK_UPLOADS=0: the compute class's inline uploads and inline
  QMDs go to a store instead of guest memory (the host GPU writes them in stream order);
  Eglantine's QMD reads, front and macro MME DMA reads patch from it; the translator's
  s.i2m tracks lines up to 4 KiB. 0 washed in 168 shots, but readers it misses run
  garbage on the host (Xid 13 SKEDCHECK / SPH): measuring only.
- EDEN_NX2_PASSTHROUGH_STAMPS=1: four-word reports carry Eglantine's GPU clock.
- EDEN_NX2_PASSTHROUGH_CATCHUP_ALL=1, _QMD_LOG=1, _HWACQ_SELF, _KEEP_NOSWITCH.
On by default: HWACQ waits when memory meets an acquire while a lowering write to that
semaphore is still pending on the host; inline uploads to known semaphores are promised
writes; a 2 s sole-mode acquire wait logs the host channels (LogStuck).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
